---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Moving to Andorra | Official residency and relocation notes"
  description="How a serious move to Andorra is organised: official immigration routes on Govern.ad, housing, banking and counsel. Hedged. Not legal advice."
  path="/moving-to-andorra"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Moving to Andorra</h1>
    <p>
      A move is an immigration file, a place to live, a bank, and usually local
      counsel. This is an orientation from official pages — not a quote, and
      not a tax plan.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Quotas, fees and financial conditions change. We do not repeat amounts.
        Read the live text on
        <a
          href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Govern.ad — residència i treball</a
        >
        and
        <a
          href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">residència</a
        >
        before you act.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>From where you are leaving</h2>
    <p>
      The permit types are Andorran. What changes is the document you present
      and whether a bilateral convention applies. The Government publishes a
      2001 convention with Spain and France on entry, circulation and
      establishment, and a later convention with Portugal. Confirm your own
      nationality on the current immigration pages. Official letter codes
      (A.1, J.1, D.1, B.1) and a practitioner A/B/C/D map are on
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>.
    </p>
    <div class="official-links">
      <a href="/moving-to-andorra-from-the-uk">Moving from the United Kingdom</a>
      <a href="/moving-to-andorra-from-spain">Moving from Spain</a>
      <a href="/moving-to-andorra-from-france">Moving from France</a>
    </div>

    <h2>The file itself</h2>
    <p>
      Applications go to the Servei d’Immigració. Official pages describe
      identity documents, apostilled or legalised criminal-record certificates,
      proof of accommodation, civil-status documents, and — for workers — a
      contract. A medical review is part of the published file. After a grant,
      you register with the Comú of the parish. Detail is on
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Remote workers should read the Government’s
      <a href="/digital-nomad">D.3 digital-nomad page note</a>
      rather than a brochure. Residence without local employment is
      <a href="/residence-without-work">D.1</a>.
      Self-employed activity is
      <a href="/self-employed-residence">J.1</a>.
      Family files are
      <a href="/family-reunification">B.1</a>.
      None of those is
      <a href="/tax-residence">tax residence</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Housing, banks, counsel</h2>
    <p>
      Buying as a non-resident is a separate authorisation from a residence
      permit. See
      <a href="/buying-property">buying property</a>.
      Daily banking is local and supervised:
      <a href="/opening-a-bank-account">opening a bank account</a>.
      Named firms with official sites are in the
      <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not a law firm. If you want an introduction, register below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm
    intro="Leave your details if you are considering a move. We’ll be in touch regarding residency and trusted advisors."
    source="moving-to-andorra"
  />
</Base>
